# ORM

## Framework semantics

The CakePHP ORM centers on Tables, Entities, associations, `SelectQuery`, finders, and marshaling via `newEntity`/`patchEntity`.

## Required behavior

- Compose queries; prefer custom finders for reusable semantics.
- Prevent N+1 with deliberate `contain` / join strategies.
- Distinguish filtering associations (`matching` / joinWith) from eager loading (`contain`).
- Do not assume bulk updates run entity callbacks/rules.

## Anti-patterns

- Hidden N+1
- Over-eager contain
- Eloquent-style mental models (not Laravel)

## Review checklist

- [ ] Query composable and intentional
- [ ] Association loading justified
- [ ] Lifecycle implications understood for writes